silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_25_six_step_bridge_deep_dives_sections_02_presheaf_six_step_concrete_anchor_1#localsection_over_mittens silm:hasLongDescription "The LocalSection_over_Mittens is a local section of F over Mittens: F(Mittens) = \"this specific cat (microchip 985112345678901) has 4.2 kg body mass, white-and-grey fur\". In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'LocalSection_over_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
